ac3.library/--background--                         ac3.library/--background--

    PURPOSE
        Decodes ATSC A/52 audio (Dolby Digital, AC-3: DVDs, transport
        streams, .ac3 files) to 16-bit signed PCM in the CPU's byte order
        (big-endian), interleaved. Any program may use it.

        ac3.library is the integer build (68020 and up, no FPU). On a
        68040 or 68060 with an FPU, open ac3fpu.library (AC3FPUNAME) first:
        the same functions, in floating point, faster there. ac3.library
        is not for a 68060.

    USE
        One decoder (Ac3Open) per stream. Find a frame's start (Ac3Find,
        or Ac3SyncInfo on bytes you know start one), gather its
        ai_FrameBytes bytes, and Ac3Decode them into AC3_FRAME_SAMPLES
        samples a channel. A decoder is used by one task at a time;
        different decoders may be used by different tasks at once.

        Each frame's sample rate (48000, 44100 or 32000 Hz) is in its
        header; it does not change within a stream in practice.

    MEMORY
        About 30 KB a decoder, from exec (MEMF_ANY). No stack beyond
        2 KB is needed.

    LICENCE
        The library: GPL-2.0-or-later (liba52 inside; its source comes with
        it). This interface (the headers, the .sfd, this document): MIT.

ac3.library/Ac3Close                                     ac3.library/Ac3Close

    NAME
        Ac3Close -- a decoder freed (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        Ac3Close(ac3)
                 A0
        VOID Ac3Close(APTR);

    FUNCTION
        Frees a decoder from Ac3Open. NULL is ignored.

ac3.library/Ac3Decode                                   ac3.library/Ac3Decode

    NAME
        Ac3Decode -- one frame decoded (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        samples = Ac3Decode(ac3, frame, pcm, info)
        D0                  A0   A1     A2   A3
        LONG Ac3Decode(APTR, CONST UBYTE *, WORD *, struct Ac3Info *);

    FUNCTION
        Decodes the whole frame starting at frame (all of its
        ai_FrameBytes bytes must be there) into pcm: AC3_FRAME_SAMPLES
        samples for each output channel (Ac3Open's mode: 2, or 1 for
        AC3_MONO), interleaved left, right. A mono stream decoded to
        stereo gives both channels alike.

    INPUTS
        ac3   - the decoder
        frame - the frame's first byte (its sync word, 0x0B77)
        pcm   - AC3_FRAME_SAMPLES * 2 WORDs (or * 1 for AC3_MONO)
        info  - filled with the frame's header and ai_OutChannels; or NULL

    RESULT
        AC3_FRAME_SAMPLES; or AC3E_SYNC (no frame header there: nothing
        written), AC3E_CORRUPT (the frame did not decode: pcm is silence,
        and the next frame decodes as usual), AC3E_ARGS.

ac3.library/Ac3Find                                       ac3.library/Ac3Find

    NAME
        Ac3Find -- the first frame header in a buffer (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        offset = Ac3Find(buf, len, info)
        D0               A0   D0   A1
        LONG Ac3Find(CONST UBYTE *, LONG, struct Ac3Info *);

    FUNCTION
        Looks through len bytes for a valid frame header (a sync word and
        a header that makes sense) and returns its offset, filling info
        (if not NULL). The frame itself may go on past len.

    RESULT
        The offset, or -1 if none starts in the buffer (keep its last
        AC3_HEADER - 1 bytes and look again with more).

ac3.library/Ac3Open                                       ac3.library/Ac3Open

    NAME
        Ac3Open -- a new decoder (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        ac3 = Ac3Open(mode, flags)
        D0            D0    D1
        APTR Ac3Open(ULONG, ULONG);

    FUNCTION
        A decoder for one stream, decoding to mode's channels:
            AC3_STEREO  two (the stream's channels mixed down as A/52 says)
            AC3_MONO    one
            AC3_DOLBY   two, Dolby Surround (Pro Logic) compatible
        flags:
            AC3F_NODRC  the stream's dynamic range compression (which
                        evens out a film's loud and quiet parts for small
                        speakers) not applied

    RESULT
        The decoder, or NULL (no memory, or an unknown mode).

ac3.library/Ac3SyncInfo                               ac3.library/Ac3SyncInfo

    NAME
        Ac3SyncInfo -- a frame's header read (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        bytes = Ac3SyncInfo(buf, info)
        D0                  A0   A1
        LONG Ac3SyncInfo(CONST UBYTE *, struct Ac3Info *);

    FUNCTION
        Reads the AC3_HEADER bytes at buf as a frame header.

    RESULT
        The frame's length in bytes (info filled, if not NULL), or 0 if
        buf does not start a frame.

ac3.library/Ac3Version                                 ac3.library/Ac3Version

    NAME
        Ac3Version -- the library's description (V1)

    SYNOPSIS
        text = Ac3Version()
        D0
        CONST_STRPTR Ac3Version(void);

    RESULT
        For example "ac3 1.0, liba52 0.8.0, integer".
